          "id": "q-know-it-1",
          "order": 1,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We typically like to think of ourselves as easy to love, don't we? When is a time maybe you haven't been the easiest to love? How has God grown you since then?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-know-it-2",
          "order": 2,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "• What do you notice about God in these verses?"
            }
          ],
          "lead": [
            {
              "segments": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Read "
                },
                {
                  "type": "scripture",
                  "displayText": "Romans 5:8-11",
                  "reference": {
                    "book": "Romans",
                    "bookId": "ROM",
                    "chapter": 5,
                    "verseStart": 8,
                    "verseEnd": 11
                  },
                  "references": [
                    {
                      "book": "Romans",
                      "bookId": "ROM",
                      "chapter": 5,
                      "verseStart": 8,
                      "verseEnd": 11
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " In verse 10 Paul says our friendship with God was restored by Jesus' death...while we were still His enemies! He goes on to remind us that it's only because of Jesus' death and resurrection we can be saved and enjoy friendship with God."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "segments": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Read "
                },
                {
